WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.413
What does Learn leave to you?

2
00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:04.052
One GCC sentence covers the whole product,

3
00:00:04.052 --> 00:00:08.426
so nothing says anything per feature,
and preview features are silent.

4
00:00:08.426 --> 00:00:11.905
License names come without
service plan identifiers,

5
00:00:11.905 --> 00:00:14.225
so a script can't match a license by ID.

6
00:00:14.225 --> 00:00:19.175
The onboarding read is beta, and
beta APIs are subject to change.

7
00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:21.438
And nothing covers the decision itself.

8
00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:23.923
So the kit adds an availability table,

9
00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:28.733
one row per feature with an interim
path where GCC isn't stated; a decision

10
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:33.863
record that names the SKU the agency reads
from its own export; and nine checks.

11
00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:38.210
The verdict: keep Learn's statements
as they are, and build what it leaves.
